🚀 Day 10 of #DrGViswanathanChallenge

Today, I solved LeetCode 240 – Search a 2D Matrix II.

This problem helped me understand an elegant searching technique that takes advantage of the matrix's sorted rows and columns. Instead of using Binary Search on every row, I learned how to eliminate an entire row or column in a single step.

💡 Approach: Staircase Search (Top-Right Traversal)

I started from the top-right corner of the matrix.

If the current element was equal to the target, I returned true.
If the target was smaller, I moved left since all elements below were even larger.
If the target was greater, I moved down since all elements to the left were smaller.

By eliminating one row or one column in every iteration, I efficiently searched the matrix without checking every element.

📚 What I Learned:
✅ Understanding the Staircase Search technique
✅ Leveraging row-wise and column-wise sorted properties
✅ Eliminating an entire row or column in each step
✅ Choosing the right starting point for efficient traversal
✅ Achieving an optimized O(m + n) time complexity with O(1) extra space

